
cron --> 
   it keeps running as a job, it fetches the jobs to execute.
    ✅ function triggerExecutor() ==> fetches job which need to be run as their nextExecutionTime <= currentTime. 


triggerScheduler() --> 
   create and stored job for a trigger in mongodb.

    ✅ triggerJobSchema --> {
     _id: ObjectId,
     
     title : "morning reminder job..."    // a title to identify the purpose of the job

     userId: 123,                  // Owner of job
     
     type: "one_time" | "recurring",
     
     recuring : true|false, 

     purpose: "morning_planning" | "night_reflection" | "custom_reminder",
     
     cronPattern: "0 9 * * *" | null,      // Used for recurring jobs

     timezone: "Asia/Kolkata",      // Always store this

     actionType: "runAgent" | "sendMessage",    // What should happen

     payload: {         // payload or parameters for that action type
       message: "Reminder: Call mom", or
       instruction: "Generate morning schedule for user"
     },

     status: "active" | "processing" | "completed" | "failed" | "cancelled",  // Execution state

     attempts: 0,                    // Retry count
     maxAttempts: 3,

     lastExecutedAt: Date | null,
     nextExecutionAt: Date | null,          // IMPORTANT for recurring

     expiryDate : Date | null,      // date after which job will be permanently inactive

     failedAt: Date,                 // in case if job failes. 

     createdAt: Date,
     updatedAt: Date
   }

   function createTriggerJob() => created a job in mongodb with this schema. 
            updateTriggerJob(title/id, body) => in case any existing job needs to be updated eithe by title or id. 


triggerExecutor() --> 
   fetched jobs which need to execute and execute function according to it. 

   it will fetch the jobs from mongodb with a filter ==>

   that will return the list of the jobs which needs to be executed. [ 1230, 1231....]

   call execution function with updating the status of the job = PROCESSING 
      each jobs will have a action type ==> call that actiontype(payload). 

   if job is sucessfully completed
      update the job in mongodb.
      attempts = 0 
         if recuring is true or not =>
            status = ACTIVE 
            lastExecutedAt : currentTime; 
            nextExecutionAt : predict the next execution by current time + cron.
         if recuring is false =? 
            stauts = COMPLETE 
            lastExecutedAt : currentTime;
            nextExecutionAt : null 

         if expiry <= currentTime 
            status = COMPLETE 
            nextExecutionAt : null 


   if job was not completed due to error in actiontype(payload): 
      if attempts < maxAttempts 
         attempts++ 
         again call the function to execute this job. 

      else 
         update the job in mongodb. 
         lockedAt : currentTime
         sendMessage("job with this purpose was failed at this time with this error")

   function executeTriggerJob(id) => execute the job, call the action and update mongo accordingly




